# ─── JEV cron-triage — a CONFIGURABLE trigger, not a fixed cadence ───────────
#
# There is NO hardcoded interval. The number below is an EXAMPLE policy choice
# (`*/5` = every 5 minutes) — change it to match your workload. A busy service
# might run every minute; a slow queue every 30. The `triage` pack decides
# whether the tick actually WAKES an agent, so a fast cadence is cheap: most
# ticks resolve to SLEEP.
#
# Install with:  crontab -e   (then paste one line)
#
# Interval trigger (universal: any host with cron):
*/5 * * * * cd /path/to/repo && JEV_TRIAGE_INTERVAL_MS=300000 JEV_WAKE_CMD='<your wake command>' node harness/hooks/cron-triage/wake.mjs --interval >> /var/log/jev-triage.log 2>&1
#
# Notes:
# - `JEV_TRIAGE_INTERVAL_MS` is informational context for the pack; the actual
#   cadence is this cron expression.
# - `JEV_WAKE_CMD` runs only when triage returns a blocking regression.
# - Event-based equivalent (webhook) is documented in README.md — same script,
#   invoked with `--event '<json>'` instead of `--interval`.
